{
  "page": 3,
  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "on time and stimuli. The matching performed between individual",
      "bbox": [
        58.05350112915039,
        61.439247131347656,
        297.1542663574219,
        69.66134643554688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "conditions is however often questionable, in particular if some",
      "bbox": [
        58.05350112915039,
        72.0409927368164,
        297.162353515625,
        80.26309204101562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "populations change their characteristics dramatically or are not/",
      "bbox": [
        58.05350112915039,
        82.64273834228516,
        297.1381530761719,
        90.86483764648438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "hardly",
      "bbox": [
        58.05350112915039,
        93.3010025024414,
        81.18655395507812,
        101.52310180664062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "distinguishable",
      "bbox": [
        88.49678039550781,
        93.3010025024414,
        141.7655792236328,
        101.52310180664062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "under",
      "bbox": [
        149.09912109375,
        93.3010025024414,
        170.3671875,
        101.52310180664062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "some",
      "bbox": [
        177.67202758789062,
        93.3010025024414,
        196.25021362304688,
        101.52310180664062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "condition.",
      "bbox": [
        203.523681640625,
        93.3010025024414,
        239.83721923828125,
        101.52310180664062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In",
      "bbox": [
        247.11874389648438,
        93.3010025024414,
        255.05392456054688,
        101.52310180664062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "this",
      "bbox": [
        262.3121337890625,
        93.3010025024414,
        274.9097900390625,
        101.52310180664062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "case",
      "bbox": [
        282.2110595703125,
        93.3010025024414,
        297.13995361328125,
        101.52310180664062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "matching-based methods are highly error-prone [12].",
      "bbox": [
        58.05350112915039,
        103.90274810791016,
        253.76185607910156,
        112.12484741210938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Pathway models",
      "bbox": [
        58.05350112915039,
        129.66990661621094,
        127.76680755615234,
        138.81556701660156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "To circumvent shortcomings of mixture modelling, we propose",
      "bbox": [
        67.01100158691406,
        141.54635620117188,
        297.1195068359375,
        149.76846313476562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "to complement it with pathway information. The responses of",
      "bbox": [
        58.05366897583008,
        152.20462036132812,
        297.164306640625,
        160.42672729492188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "subpopulations to different experimental conditions is ultimately",
      "bbox": [
        58.05366897583008,
        162.80636596679688,
        297.11138916015625,
        171.02847290039062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "determined by the involved metabolic, signalling and gene",
      "bbox": [
        58.05366897583008,
        173.40811157226562,
        297.1356201171875,
        181.63021850585938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "regulatory pathways. Accordingly, experimental conditions can",
      "bbox": [
        58.05366897583008,
        184.06637573242188,
        297.1499938964844,
        192.28848266601562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "be matched using models of the underlying biochemical pathway.",
      "bbox": [
        58.05366897583008,
        194.66812133789062,
        297.1401062011719,
        202.89022827148438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Biochemical pathways are mostly modelled using reaction rate",
      "bbox": [
        67.01100158691406,
        205.55319213867188,
        297.1615905761719,
        213.77529907226562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "equations (RREs) [24], which are systems of ODEs. RREs",
      "bbox": [
        58.05366897583008,
        216.15493774414062,
        297.1849365234375,
        224.37704467773438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "describe the temporal evolution of the ‘‘average state’’ of cells in a",
      "bbox": [
        58.05366897583008,
        226.75668334960938,
        297.1777648925781,
        234.97879028320312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "cell population, e.g., the abundance of signalling molecules and",
      "bbox": [
        58.05366897583008,
        237.41494750976562,
        297.1356201171875,
        245.63705444335938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "their activity, assuming that the population is homogeneous. More",
      "bbox": [
        58.05366897583008,
        248.01669311523438,
        297.1419372558594,
        256.2388000488281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "precisely, RREs implicitly assume that the variance in the",
      "bbox": [
        315.1004638671875,
        61.439674377441406,
        554.1762084960938,
        69.66177368164062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "abundance of chemical species across cells is small. Therefore,",
      "bbox": [
        315.1004638671875,
        71.9849624633789,
        554.1690063476562,
        80.20706176757812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "these models can neither be used to process the distributional",
      "bbox": [
        315.1004638671875,
        82.58670806884766,
        554.1411743164062,
        90.80880737304688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "information encoded in snapshot data nor to study cellular",
      "bbox": [
        315.1004638671875,
        93.1884536743164,
        554.1618041992188,
        101.41055297851562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "subpopulations.",
      "bbox": [
        315.1004638671875,
        103.79019927978516,
        371.5433349609375,
        112.01229858398438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "While RRE based modelling of heterogenous cell populations",
      "bbox": [
        324.05780029296875,
        114.61881256103516,
        554.1636352539062,
        122.84091186523438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "consisting of different subpopulations is not desirable, RREs might",
      "bbox": [
        315.1004638671875,
        125.2205581665039,
        554.1895751953125,
        133.44265747070312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "be used to model the dynamics of rather homogeneous subpop-",
      "bbox": [
        315.1004638671875,
        135.82229614257812,
        554.171630859375,
        144.04440307617188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ulations. In the following, we will describe the ‘‘average dynamics’’",
      "bbox": [
        315.1004638671875,
        146.42404174804688,
        554.1868896484375,
        154.64614868164062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "of cells in the i-th subpopulation using a RRE,",
      "bbox": [
        315.1004638671875,
        156.56585693359375,
        487.27410888671875,
        165.19143676757812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "_xi~f (xi,ji,u),",
      "bbox": [
        348.9464416503906,
        182.24517822265625,
        401.52008056640625,
        191.7118682861328
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "xi(0)~x0(ji,u),",
      "bbox": [
        410.5132751464844,
        182.24517822265625,
        467.907470703125,
        191.7118682861328
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "i~1, . . . ,m,",
      "bbox": [
        476.9006652832031,
        182.24517822265625,
        520.368408203125,
        190.56590270996094
      ],
