      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ð2Þ",
      "bbox": [
        542.8352661132812,
        181.94927978515625,
        554.2242431640625,
        190.9066162109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "in which xi(t)[Rnx",
      "bbox": [
        315.09930419921875,
        199.99142456054688,
        382.9666748046875,
        211.04420471191406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "z is the state of the i-th subpopulation at time t,",
      "bbox": [
        376.3841857910156,
        201.97430419921875,
        554.2042236328125,
        213.09500122070312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ji[R",
      "bbox": [
        315.0989990234375,
        215.6670684814453,
        332.81878662109375,
        225.1039581298828
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "nj",
      "bbox": [
        332.843994140625,
        211.27322387695312,
        339.10009765625,
        219.34628295898438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "z is the parameter vector of the i-th subpopulation, and",
      "bbox": [
        332.843994140625,
        215.6939697265625,
        554.185546875,
        226.24703979492188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "u(t)[Rnu is the time-dependent external stimulus. The vector field",
      "bbox": [
        315.09912109375,
        223.86459350585938,
        554.1893920898438,
        235.09115600585938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "f encodes the biochemical pathway and x0 models the depen-",
      "bbox": [
        315.09930419921875,
        237.0108642578125,
        554.1739501953125,
        246.99679565429688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "dence of the initial condition on subpopulation parameters and",
      "bbox": [
        315.0982971191406,
        248.01583862304688,
        554.178466796875,
        256.2379455566406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Figure 1. Illustration of population snapshot data and ODE constrained mixture modelling. (A) Heterogeneous population consisting of",
      "bbox": [
        58.05350112915039,
        653.5751953125,
        554.19677734375,
        660.9635620117188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "two homogeneous subpopulations with a very different response level. Snapshot data provide at different time points (filled circle) information",
      "bbox": [
        58.053497314453125,
        662.6373291015625,
        554.1895751953125,
        669.9539184570312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "about the biological state of single cells. This allows for the characterisation of the kinetics of the subpopulations using threshold, histogram and",
      "bbox": [
        58.053497314453125,
        671.5950317382812,
        554.2294921875,
        678.91162109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "kernel density estimate (KDE) based methods as well as mixture modelling. (B) Heterogeneous population consisting of two heterogenous",
      "bbox": [
        58.053466796875,
        680.552734375,
        554.1974487304688,
        687.8693237304688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "subpopulations with a large overlap of the dose response behaviour, rendering an analysis using snapshot data difficult. (C) Table including the",
      "bbox": [
        58.053466796875,
        689.5104370117188,
        554.197265625,
        696.8270263671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "available analysis tools for population snapshot data and proposed ODE constrained mixture modelling along with key properties of the methods. (D)",
      "bbox": [
        58.053466796875,
        698.4681396484375,
        554.1902465820312,
        705.7847290039062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Sketch of ODE constrained mixture modelling which combines mixture modelling of the measurement data with pathway information, thereby",
      "bbox": [
        58.053466796875,
        707.4258422851562,
        554.2422485351562,
        714.742431640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "allowing for an improved quantification of subpopulation properties and mechanistic insights.",
      "bbox": [
        58.053466796875,
        716.383544921875,
        378.62445068359375,
        723.7001342773438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
